WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.708 --> 00:00:14.018
What's up, people?

00:00:14.042 --> 00:00:16.893
First of all, I cannot believe
I'm on TED Talk.

00:00:16.917 --> 00:00:18.768
This is a big deal.

00:00:18.792 --> 00:00:20.059
Because right now,

00:00:20.083 --> 00:00:22.059
everybody in my village is watching this.

00:00:22.083 --> 00:00:24.976
And so, of course,
my bride price just went up.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.726
My name is Adeola Fayehun.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.018
I'm from Nigeria.

00:00:28.042 --> 00:00:29.309
I live in the US,

00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:31.809
I'm a journalist, or a comedian,

00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:33.184
or a satirist,

00:00:33.208 --> 00:00:34.934
anything you want me to be, really.

00:00:34.958 --> 00:00:37.393
I'm every woman, it's all in me.

00:00:37.417 --> 00:00:41.476
I host a YouTube show called
"Keeping It Real with Adeola."

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:46.518
Now this show is a gentle,
respectful and very blunt way

00:00:46.542 --> 00:00:49.101
of calling out corrupt African leaders.

00:00:49.125 --> 00:00:52.423
(Video) President Buhari: I don't know
which party my wife belongs to,

00:00:52.433 --> 00:00:54.184
but she belongs to my kitchen.

00:00:54.208 --> 00:00:55.643
Adeola Fayehun: Oh, my God!

00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:57.268
I need some water --

00:00:57.292 --> 00:00:58.583
I said I need some water!

00:01:00.833 --> 00:01:01.881
See?

00:01:01.885 --> 00:01:04.018
I basically keep it real with them, ha!

00:01:04.042 --> 00:01:06.726
Especially when they mess up,
which is a lot of times.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.643
If any African official
is watching me, by the way,

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:11.726
I'm not talking about you, sir.

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:14.726
I'm talking about your colleagues, yes.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:19.226
I do this because Africa
has everything in it to be great.

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:20.684
You know, I grew up believing

00:01:20.708 --> 00:01:23.809
that Africa as a continent is a giant.

00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:26.351
We've got skills, intellectuals,

00:01:26.375 --> 00:01:30.059
natural resources
more than any other continent.

00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:33.893
Africa supplies 31 percent
of the world's gold,

00:01:33.917 --> 00:01:35.809
manganese and uranium,

00:01:35.833 --> 00:01:38.976
57 percent of the world's diamonds

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.184
and 13 percent of the world's oil.

00:01:41.208 --> 00:01:44.184
We have no reason to depend on aid

00:01:44.208 --> 00:01:47.809
or borrowing money
from China or the World Bank.

00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:49.268
But without good leaders,

00:01:49.292 --> 00:01:53.518
we're like an eagle
that has no idea it could fly,

00:01:53.542 --> 00:01:55.351
let alone soar.

00:01:55.375 --> 00:01:57.809
Africa is a like a sleeping giant.

00:01:57.833 --> 00:02:01.184
Now the truth is,
I'm trying to wake up this giant,

00:02:01.208 --> 00:02:03.309
and that's why I air the dirty laundry

00:02:03.333 --> 00:02:05.393
of those in charge of the giant.

00:02:05.417 --> 00:02:08.143
Our politicians, our religious leaders,

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:09.893
with huge respect, of course,

00:02:09.917 --> 00:02:12.601
because more than anything else,

00:02:12.625 --> 00:02:16.268
African leaders love to be respected.

00:02:16.292 --> 00:02:18.268
So I give it to them in doses.

00:02:18.292 --> 00:02:19.559
On my show,

00:02:19.583 --> 00:02:21.351
I kneel for them -- ha! --

00:02:21.375 --> 00:02:24.143
I call them my uncles, my aunties,

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:25.726
my fathers in the lord,

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:27.268
and then --

00:02:27.292 --> 00:02:30.684
I insult them for insulting
our intelligence.

00:02:30.708 --> 00:02:32.768
And it's because we are tired

00:02:32.792 --> 00:02:36.184
of the hypocrisy and false promises.

00:02:36.208 --> 00:02:37.601
For example,

00:02:37.625 --> 00:02:41.393
the Nigerian president
vowed to end medical tourism

00:02:41.417 --> 00:02:44.101
by fixing our dilapidated hospitals

00:02:44.125 --> 00:02:46.268
and building us new ones.

00:02:46.292 --> 00:02:47.726
But what did he do?

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:52.684
He spends three months
receiving treatment in London in 2017.

00:02:52.708 --> 00:02:56.184
We were without a president
for three months.

00:02:56.208 --> 00:02:58.226
We were president-less for three months.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:00.934
So then it becomes my job
to call out the President,

00:03:00.958 --> 00:03:02.226
with respect, of course.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:05.559
I said, "Ha, Mr. President,
it's your girl, Adeola.

00:03:05.583 --> 00:03:07.559
You know how I do, 
how you doing?

00:03:07.583 --> 00:03:09.434
You have no shame."

00:03:09.458 --> 00:03:10.768
I forgot to add "sir."

00:03:10.792 --> 00:03:12.893
"Sir, you have no shame.

00:03:12.917 --> 00:03:14.678
(In Yoruba: You have no fear of God.)

00:03:14.678 --> 00:03:15.976
You have no fear of God."

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.893
Thirty-five thousand Nigerian doctors
are presently working in the US,

00:03:20.917 --> 00:03:22.351
the UK and Canada,

00:03:22.375 --> 00:03:24.018
doing amazing things,

00:03:24.042 --> 00:03:27.184
because in Nigeria,
they are not well-paid,

00:03:27.208 --> 00:03:29.351
neither do they have
the necessary equipment

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.643
to do the job of being a doctor.

00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:35.518
And this is happening
in many African countries.

00:03:35.542 --> 00:03:38.434
We have the capacity to fly.

00:03:38.458 --> 00:03:42.851
But sadly, a lot of African talent
is flying straight out of Africa

00:03:42.875 --> 00:03:44.643
to other continents.

00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:45.934
For example,

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:49.268
this Nigerian doctor
operated on an unborn baby

00:03:49.292 --> 00:03:50.559
in Texas.

00:03:50.583 --> 00:03:52.226
Also, this Nigerian doctor

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:56.809
discovered the neurological effects
of concussion on athletes.

00:03:56.833 --> 00:03:59.559
And many countries have African athletes

00:03:59.583 --> 00:04:02.601
winning the gold medal for them.

00:04:02.625 --> 00:04:04.059
The interesting thing is,

00:04:04.083 --> 00:04:06.559
we're waiting for God to fix Africa.

00:04:06.583 --> 00:04:09.536
Like, for real, it's not a joke,
we are, we're waiting for God.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.768
I mean, just look
at the president of Burundi.

00:04:11.792 --> 00:04:14.184
He's jailing journalists
and opposition members,

00:04:14.208 --> 00:04:17.101
but he declared national day of prayer

00:04:17.125 --> 00:04:20.434
so that people could pray
for God to fix the country.

00:04:20.458 --> 00:04:23.101
And I'm like, shouldn't he
be fixing the country?

00:04:23.125 --> 00:04:24.684
Oh, no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:04:24.708 --> 00:04:26.768
We want God to fix it.

00:04:26.792 --> 00:04:29.351
Do you see what I have to deal with?

00:04:29.375 --> 00:04:30.643
I'm telling you,

00:04:30.667 --> 00:04:33.809
thunder is getting ready
to hit these politicians some day.

00:04:33.833 --> 00:04:36.393
We are better than this.

00:04:36.417 --> 00:04:40.309
I want our leaders
to start taking responsibility

00:04:40.333 --> 00:04:43.809
and stop putting everything on God.

00:04:43.833 --> 00:04:46.059
God has given us everything we need.

00:04:46.083 --> 00:04:48.643
It's right here, let's use it.

00:04:48.667 --> 00:04:51.768
But here's the thing,
my favorite part of what I do

00:04:51.792 --> 00:04:54.809
is featuring Africans doing amazing work,

00:04:54.833 --> 00:04:57.059
ordinary people touching lives.

00:04:57.083 --> 00:04:59.726
Like this Kenyan woman, Wangari Maathai,

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:03.559
the first African woman
to receive the Nobel Peace prize,

00:05:03.583 --> 00:05:05.351
for standing up for human rights

00:05:05.375 --> 00:05:07.518
and planting a million trees.

00:05:07.542 --> 00:05:09.684
Also this Zimbabwean woman,

00:05:09.708 --> 00:05:11.101
Dr. Tererai Trent,

00:05:11.125 --> 00:05:14.476
who was married off at the age of 14

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.226
in exchange for a cow.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:19.268
Yet, this woman taught herself
to read and write,

00:05:19.292 --> 00:05:21.309
and she ended up on Oprah's show.

00:05:21.333 --> 00:05:24.851
Oh, Father, I want
to be on Oprah some day.

00:05:24.875 --> 00:05:26.893
Today, this woman has built schools

00:05:26.917 --> 00:05:29.643
for thousands of children in Zimbabwe.

00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:33.601
Also, popular British architect
David Adjaye has designed

00:05:33.625 --> 00:05:36.393
spectacular buildings around the world.

00:05:36.417 --> 00:05:39.184
And he's both Ghanian and Tanzanian,

00:05:39.208 --> 00:05:43.268
so we know that it has to be
the Ghanian Jollof rice,

00:05:43.292 --> 00:05:44.559
which he ate,

00:05:44.583 --> 00:05:46.601
that gave him the inspiration to design.

00:05:46.625 --> 00:05:48.553
Ah, maybe it's the Nigerian Jollof rice,

00:05:48.577 --> 00:05:50.069
because Nigerian one is better.

00:05:50.094 --> 00:05:52.863
Anyway, but that is what gave him
the inspiration to become

00:05:52.888 --> 00:05:55.101
the great man that he is today.

00:05:55.125 --> 00:05:56.684
And while I have your attention,

00:05:56.708 --> 00:05:58.143
I have one more thing to say,

00:05:58.167 --> 00:05:59.434
so please move closer.

00:05:59.458 --> 00:06:01.809
OK, that's good,
don't get too close, that's good.

00:06:01.833 --> 00:06:03.518
I don't like the way some of you

00:06:03.542 --> 00:06:05.351
portray Africa.

00:06:05.375 --> 00:06:06.976
Not all of you, just some of you.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.268
You especially.

00:06:08.292 --> 00:06:11.101
First of all, it's not a country,
it's a continent.

00:06:11.125 --> 00:06:13.434
I do not know Paul from Uganda,

00:06:13.458 --> 00:06:15.559
I don't know Rebecca from Zimbabwe.

00:06:15.583 --> 00:06:17.643
Nigeria is as far from Zimbabwe

00:06:17.667 --> 00:06:20.018
as New York is from France.

00:06:20.042 --> 00:06:23.184
And it's not a bunch of naked people
in need of Western charity.

00:06:23.208 --> 00:06:24.976
You have it all wrong.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.351
Lions are not roaming our streets, OK?

00:06:27.375 --> 00:06:28.643
And I could go on,

00:06:28.667 --> 00:06:30.768
but you already know
what I'm talking about.

00:06:30.792 --> 00:06:32.184
So while I try to do my job,

00:06:32.208 --> 00:06:34.476
trying to wake up
the sleeping giant, Africa,

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:37.476
so she could take her rightful place
on the world's arena,

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.226
you can your bit, too.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:41.559
Please listen more.

00:06:41.583 --> 00:06:43.643
Listen to your African friends

00:06:43.667 --> 00:06:45.518
without a preconceived notion

00:06:45.542 --> 00:06:48.726
of what you think
that they're going to say.

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:50.559
Read African books.

00:06:50.583 --> 00:06:53.018
Oh, my God, watch African movies.

00:06:53.042 --> 00:06:54.434
Or at the very least,

00:06:54.458 --> 00:06:57.851
learn some of the names
of our 54 beautiful countries.

00:06:57.875 --> 00:07:01.101
That's right, 54, baby, five-four.

00:07:01.125 --> 00:07:02.643
Alright, y'all, it's been real,

00:07:02.667 --> 00:07:04.620
and I'm keeping it real right up in here.

00:07:04.644 --> 00:07:06.893
Until next time,
I'm going to see you all later.

00:07:06.917 --> 00:07:08.250
Peace out.

